WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.230
More importantly, don't forget 
about the regular meet.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.490
"Regular meet"?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.950
It's a regularly scheduled 
competition where quiz teams

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.410
from several schools come together.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.630
Well, that means you have 
a rival, doesn't it?

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.370
A... rival?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.420
Yep.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.030
S-Sorry!

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.770
I'm going home!

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.710
Koshiyama-kun?

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.260
<i>"Rival"...</i>

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.770
<i>That's a title you only give to one 
whose skills you acknowledge,</i>

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.480
<i>evoking more passion 
than anyone else's name.</i>

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.390
<i>I always thought it'd never be more
 than a dream for me to have one.</i>

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.150
<b>Imperial University
Quiz Bowl Studies 
No. 1 in Japanese 
Quiz Bowl</b>

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:55.980
Yeah!

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.280
It's no dream!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.170
<b>Question 7: "...Their Past Quiz Questions"</b>

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.550
<b>Club Competition</b>

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.550
<b>Paper</b>

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.550
The regular meet?

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.080
Mikuriya-kun told me about it.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.550
We figured you'd know the schedule,

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.500
and how the tournament works, and so on.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.560
Jinko, work more quietly.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:47.560
Sure.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.570
I was just thinking I should 
tell you all about it.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.310
The full schedule is still 
to be confirmed,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.530
but the regular meet will take place in 
June at Asagaoka Girls' High School.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.210
Asagaoka?

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.990
That's Yukicchi's school!

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.450
The "regular meet"

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:08.660
is, in fact, a normal activity 
for every quiz bowl team.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.430
But the "regular meet" for 
student quiz bowl teams

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.140
is basically a meet held 
out of school hours.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.330
Schools take turns 
hosting a quiz tournament.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.890
You could call it a larger version 
of the last meet at Sekigawata.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.640
A larger version...

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.740
All the strongest schools in Kanto and 
the surrounding prefectures participate.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.970
Kaijou Academy will most
 likely be there, as well.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.370
Kaijou's that elite high school!

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.610
Oh, gosh! All those smart 
boys will be coming <i>here</i>!

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.160
As Asagaoka is the host school,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.120
we must make preparations to welcome 
these competitive schools.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:49.540
So we'll get to make boys from competitive 
schools really apply themselves!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.040
And we get to put anguished looks on 
their faces with our tough questions!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.380
It'll be a white-hot drama of 
boys in a garden of girls!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.340
Uh, I think there'll be 
girls participating, too...

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.300
I've already come up with a special plan.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.770
Sekigawata, Miyaura... and Kaijou, too?

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:15.710
Kaijou's quiz team is the 
toughest of the tough.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.730
They're a top national level team.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:19.740
Seriously?

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.240
Participation is optional.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.800
I'm in!

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:24.810
Me, too!

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.910
M-Me, too!

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.520
<i>I'm going up against Mikuriya-kun.</i>

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:34.790
Good. In competitive quiz bowl, you 
can't get better without experience.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.790
It'll be good for you to get some practice 
with veteran schools at the regular meet.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:43.510
C'mon, Gakuto. Sounds like y'all are 
expectin' to lose right from the get-go.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.360
Competitions're all a matter of chance. 
They're fun 'cause no one knows what'll happen.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.760
Ain't that what you're always sayin'?

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.670
That's right, Senpai!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:57.520
I think, in terms of knowledge, Koshiyama-kun 
can hold his own against those tough schools!

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.150
I-I'll do my best to win!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.960
I see.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.790
In that case, in preparation for the meet,

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.780
you should compete among 
yourselves, starting today.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.160
We'll start with a quiz paper.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.700
You have ten minutes.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:18.420
It's typical for quiz papers to be issued 
during the early rounds of the meet.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:22.770
It's a quiz format that 
simply tests knowledge.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:24.630
Begin.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.920
<i>So written quizzes are part 
of competitions, too?</i>

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.740
<i>This might play to my strengths.</i>

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.920
<i>Or maybe it won't be so easy...</i>

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:37.600
<b>Shoudo Island</b>

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:37.600
<b>Trench coat</b>

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:37.600
<b>Tumbleweed</b>

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.600
<i>Fifty questions in ten minutes... 
So I need to answer one every twelve seconds.</i>

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.190
<i>Time limits put you under pressure,</i>

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.700
<i>and answers don't always 
spring to mind immediately.</i>

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.660
42. The fish known as the "harbinger of spring" is the Pacific herring... 
43. Meaning "long shirt," the Vietnamese outfit... 
44. One of the world's three rarest delicacies, caviar, refers to the eggs of... 
45. Often seen in logo designs of fashion brands, a sketched pattern... 
46. In 1935, the novel <i>Sobo</i> won the Akutagawa Prize for which...

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:47.660
<i>Plus, I have trouble with 
categories I'm less familiar with.</i>

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.680
<i>The last question is...</i>

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:53.640
<i>"How much does Sasajima Jinko 
currently weigh, in kilos?"</i>

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.160
A question requiring 
approximation is often added

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.920
at the end of quizzes to determine 
a winner in the event of a tie.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.920
<b>Approximation Question 
How much does Sasajima Jinko currently weigh, in kilos?</b>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.670
<i>The issue is those boobs...</i>

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.130
<i>They're definitely heavier than mine.</i>

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.140
<i>She's taller than me...</i>

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:14.100
What? What's up with y'all? Stop starin' at me!

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.350
That's ten minutes. Time's up.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.100
Get on.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.190
Why the heck?!

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.070
47.5 kilograms.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:22.730
Yeah!

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:25.030
Gakuto, you idiot!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.520
In last place with 16 points,

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.650
Inoue Daisuke.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.380
And I guessed her precise weight and all...

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.470
You have a long way to go.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.040
I-I know that!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.070
In second place with 39 points,

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:39.990
Fukami Mari.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:46.250
Aren't classic questions your strong suit? 
You'd lose in the opening round with that.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.630
I'm sorry.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.510
In first place with 44 points,

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.530
Koshiyama Shiki.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:52.010
Y-Yes, sir.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.980
I figured it'd be Koshiyama-kun.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:58.280
Koshiyama, how do you feel about your score?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.600
I-I did fairly well, I guess...

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.300
You're naïve.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.990
Every single one of the veteran school's 
players would ace a quiz of classics like this.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.370
You'd lose in the opening round, too.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.150
You wouldn't even get to 
the buzzer rounds.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.740
Whoa, harsh...

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:20.430
Paper quizzes screen out a
large number of participants.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.130
One point can separate winners from losers.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.910
Your knowledge base extends 
no further than literature.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:31.340
You won't be causing any upsets 
against the veteran schools.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.230
Senpai, you didn't need to go that far...

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.550
I know that!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:39.970
<i>If I go to the regular meet like this, 
I'll only disappoint Mikuriya-kun.</i>

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.290
I'll gain lots more knowledge!

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.150
I'll improve my technique 
and learn about quiz bowl!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:47.990
Gaudí!

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.070
Correct.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:50.940
Foyer!

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.030
Joseki!

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:54.240
Next time...

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.100
Koshiyama-kun!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.730
Focus more on the determining points.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.110
It's too late if you wait to know 
the answer before buzzing!

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.210
Buzz in as soon as you think you can guess it.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.170
Otherwise, you won't even 
get the right to answer!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:07.950
<i>Fukami-san...</i>

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:15.560
Question.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.630
The shrine where you would find the 
 god of protection against fire is—

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.220
Akihabara!

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.200
Correct.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.400
<b>Q. The shrine where you would find the god of protection against fire is 
the namesake of which town, famous for its "Electric Town"?    A. Akihabara</b>

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.190
Koshiyama

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.910
Should've known Fukami-san would kick 
our butts in the fastest finger round.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.860
Yeah, I only managed to 
get the last question.

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.410
Still...

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.860
I never knew there were so many 
quiz nuts like Gakuto out there.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.950
Didn't your brother's involvement 
in quiz bowl rub off on you at all?

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:52.880
I'm more interested in makin' things 
than answerin' questions, that's all.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.050
Oh...

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.800
The buzzers'll be done soon, too.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.500
Look forward to 'em.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:03.030
Gakuto! Wait up! Give me a ride!

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:06.480
Those two sure are close.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.330
Hey, Fukami-san...

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.620
Thanks for your advice on buzzing in.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.840
Not at all.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:19.160
Seeing you trying so hard
 motivated me, too.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:24.440
By the way, what made 
you get into quiz bowl?

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:25.870
I wanna know, too!

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.600
Well...

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.340
I guess it was my brother's influence.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.550
You have a brother?

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:38.130
Yeah. He's a year older than me,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.690
and he's been doing quiz 
bowl since middle school.

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:45.380
I always used to read quiz books like he did,

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.640
and got him to teach me about quiz bowl.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.520
Question.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:53.280
French for "flash of lightning,"

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.030
a long, thin pastry topped with 
chocolate is known by what name?

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.580
The answer is...

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:03.960
...éclair.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.560
Every year at my brother's school festival,

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.420
the quiz team hosts a quiz bowl tournament.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.340
<b>Kaijou Festival</b>

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:15.420
I eventually started taking part in it.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.340
<b>Quiz Meet 
Applications</b>

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.340
<b>As the number of 
participants is limited, 
entrants will be 
selected by lottery.</b>

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:24.660
My brother's school quiz 
team has a long history,

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.640
so the school festival's annual quiz meet

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.310
was so popular that it was 
always standing-room only.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.590
And other than me, all the 
participants were adults.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:38.670
Donkey!

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.660
Correct.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.010
Ringside seats.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:41.870
Correct.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.030
Siphon.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:43.900
Correct.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.610
Back then, I seriously regretted entering.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:52.040
I managed to get into the meet, but 
couldn't answer a single question.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.750
But in the middle of all that...

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.260
Question.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.760
French for "flash of lightning,"

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.590
a long, thin pastry topped with—

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.660
Eclair.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.130
Correct.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.740
I think it's because of that one question

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.500
that I'm in quiz bowl right now.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.980
I was only able to answer one question,

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.880
but I still can't forget that moment.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:39.970
<i>I see... Just like me and </i>Das Gemeine.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:45.850
And the other reason was the way 
my brother looked that day.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.820
Middle school first-year, Fukami Seiji.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.560
I won't lose to the older students.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:57.230
The timed fastest finger round 
will last five minutes.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.630
Now, begin.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.710
Question.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:05.530
When an airplane exceeds the speed 
of sound, the shock waves—

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:06.780
Sonic boom.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.410
<b>Q. When an airplane exceeds the speed of sound, the shock waves 
produce a sound known by what name?    A. Sonic boom</b>

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:07.960
Correct.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:13.240
The César Award.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.010
Nue.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.340
Space chorus.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.320
Correct.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.450
It was amazing.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:31.400
From what you just said, that school's 
quiz team must be pretty awesome, too.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.060
What school does your brother go to?

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.350
Well, my brother is...

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.020
a second-year at Kaijou High School.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.510
Kaijou?!

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.500
That elite high school?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:46.030
Maybe you two will face each other 
in competition at the regional meet!

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.250
Unfortunately, he won't be 
participating in the regular meet.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.160
Huh? Why not?

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.350
He quit quiz bowl.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.810
He said he wants to focus 
on his entrance exams.

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:02.750
Can't help that, right?

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:04.950
Mari?

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.140
It <i>is</i> you, Mari.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.310
Are you heading home?

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.390
Who are these two?

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:11.630
Um...

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.280
This is Koshiyama-kun and 
Inoue-kun, from my class.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.270
Our club ran late,
so they're walking with me.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:20.230
I see. Thank you for that.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.060
N-No problem.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:23.060
You're, um...

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.200
It's nice to meet you.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.160
I'm Mari's older brother, Seiji.

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.510
N-Nice to meet you!

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.370
<b>Handsome 
Big Brother</b>

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.440
<i>What a handsome big brother!</i>

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.370
<i>Only Fukami-san could 
have a brother like that!</i>

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.690
Let's go home, Mari.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.160
See you, Koshiyama-kun, Inoue-kun.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.970
S-Sure...

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.920
L-Later, then.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.240
You're back pretty early today.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:58.100
We only had one lesson at cram school.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.330
Are you always this late getting home?

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.070
Can't say I like it.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:06.450
Um... I sort of got to 
talking with my friends...

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.380
I didn't realize...

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.100
you'd joined a club.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.370
Which club?

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:18.600
You're not going to tell me you joined 
that quiz bowl circle, I hope.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:23.880
What did I tell you?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:29.090
Competing in quiz bowl is pointless.

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.980
<b>Tweeeeet</b>

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.980
<b>Toooot</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Notice Board</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Search Posts [0]</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Back to Homepage</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Asagaoka Regular Meet Details — Asagaoka, Sonohara</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>The details for the regular meet at Asagaoka have been confirmed.</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Date: June 3 (Sun.)     10:00 doors open      10:30 start 
Location: Asagaoka Girls' High School 
Campus, B Building (see URL below)</b>

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:41.650
So it's set.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.860
I'm glad it's after our midterms.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.990
That'll be tough...

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:50.700
Why did they pick that date?!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.850
That's two days before our midterms!

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:54.450
Why does only our school have exams then?!

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.510
Well, we can't do anything about it now.

00:14:57.510 --> 00:14:59.370
Everyone who'd like to 
enter, raise your hands.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:07.550
Mikuriya? Won't you need to study?

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.800
Nah.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:12.930
Midterms are no big deal if 
you've been listening in class.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.060
You're the only participant, as of right now.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.290
Relax, Mikuriya. We won't 
let you do it all alone.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.900
Maruyama, you're gonna participate, too?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.120
Just think about it. This kind of
 chance doesn't come along often.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.240
It's at an all-girls school, you 
know! A garden of sweet fruit!

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.280
That's right! It's gonna 
smell amazing, for sure!

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.750
<b>Small Classroom B</b>

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:41.500
The regular meet will take place 
on the first Sunday of next month.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.220
Read all of these by then.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:46.500
All of these in half a month?

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:52.490
Competing in quiz bowl is pointless.

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:56.910
<i>How can he call it pointless?</i>

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.300
Well, I did completely 
screw up the paper quiz.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.410
I guess I should read up a little.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.440
This is only a fraction of what I have.

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.630
I regularly collect past 
questions from other schools

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:12.240
as well as question collections 
from adult quiz circles.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.190
Whoa, they're all packed 
with nothing but words!

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.840
This looks right up your alley, Koshiyama...

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.600
You have way too many 
of those strewn about.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:30.880
Huh? Ah... I was looking for 
something, and this just happened...

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.250
What were you reading?

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:34.590
Well...

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.100
<b>Kyoto</b>

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.100
A Kyoto guide?

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:37.970
Are you going on a trip or something?

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:45.460
No, but these often have a lot of 
information on local history and landmarks.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:48.570
I thought it might be useful 
for quiz bowl, too.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.400
<b>Nara</b>

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:55.740
So you've been reading guides from all 
the regions of Kansai for that reason?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:52.610
<b>Kobe</b>

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:52.610
<b>Osaka</b>

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.500
Yeah. It's hard to stop once you start.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:01.040
I get sidetracked sometimes...

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:02.620
That's a good reading method.

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.350
It's easier to recall knowledge you took in

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:09.460
by reading related sources than by 
just reading anything at random.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.020
Will that be useful for quiz bowl?

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.830
Famous locations and local specialties 
are often used for questions.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.180
Huh?

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:17.160
Question.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.390
Huh?!

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.650
Something's come up.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:37.780
Senpai, why did you get 
involved in quiz bowl?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:43.040
Why am I in quiz bowl? 
That's a silly question.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:48.130
Do you need a reason for 
doing what you love?

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:03.680
Sasajima-senpai is so amazing...

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:05.230
Huh?!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.690
What kind of flag just triggered?!

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.270
That's right! The reason 
doesn't even matter!

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:11.770
Sorry about that.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:16.470
I love what I love, 
and I'll say it with pride!

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:17.450
I...

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.410
...love quiz bowl!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:22.660
Huh?!

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:27.040
I dunno what's goin' on, but well said!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.000
Jinko-san...

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:32.900
In response to all of y'all's enthusiasm,

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:36.220
I'd like to present my handmade buzzer set!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.590
They're done?

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.470
When did that happen?

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.430
Just a moment ago.

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:43.890
There!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:48.510
Huh?

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.600
Lunch boxes?

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:53.930
Th-They're very cute buzzer buttons.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.990
Well, let's start with a buzzer test.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:58.700
Meow!

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.030
Oink!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.060
Baa!

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.210
Ribbit!

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:03.660
I don't think so!

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.200
They're cute, but...

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.070
This'll make me forget any 
answers I come up with...

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.140
Fix this by tomorrow.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.670
Aw, y'all are no fun.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.000
Oh, yeah! Question!

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:18.670
What's a cute girl like me 
called in the Kyoto dialect?

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.270
Meow!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.050
B-Belle.

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:25.230
Dummy!

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.520
Correct!

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:29.290
It was the right answer, but 
I still got called a dummy...

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.990
<i>We finally got our own buzzers.</i>

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.430
<i>Our preparations for the regular 
meet are finally underway.</i>

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.470
Looks like just about all 
of the entries are in.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.290
Hey, Onee-tama! Look at me!

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.240
Huh?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.800
What do you think?

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.510
Hey, that's—

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.630
See? It's a perfect fit!

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.500
It's almost time for our
summer uniforms, right?

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.850
Lend me this outfit when
 summer comes around!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.870
What would you even do with it?

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:12.600
Take it off!

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.000
I guess it won't work,
since we go to different schools.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:17.220
You think <i>that's</i> the reason?

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.950
By the way, Nee-chan,

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.840
is doing quiz bowl with 
all the other kids fun?

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:27.330
Your school has a perfectly 
fine quiz bowl team.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.240
Why don't you give it a try?

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.760
But clubs are such a hassle.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.850
I've found someone interesting, though.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.500
His name's "Koshiyama."

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.300
Koshiyama? I've heard that name somewhere...

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.260
He does quiz bowl, too.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.010
Is he that literary nut from Buzou?

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:52.770
<b>Tani Kazuyoshi 
Sasajima Gakuto 
Fukami Mari 
Koshiyama Shiki 
Inoue Daisuke 
Ashiya Yousuke 
Maruyama Wataru</b>

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:52.770
He's put his name down for the regular
 meet. But how do <i>you </i>know him?

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.990
Our usual quiz master has made 
his way to a certain location.

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:36.500
Now, live from the scene: Quiz Master!

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:41.680
Yes! I'm currently in the place all high 
school students dream of visiting: New York!

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:44.890
And the venue for this year's high 
school quiz meet is, of course, right here...

00:22:44.890 --> 00:22:46.880
In front of the Statue of Liberty!

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:49.720
I'd love to go there!

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:53.470
Yes, I look forward to seeing you 
here one day, Koshiyama-kun.

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:56.870
Let's all do it together! The password is...

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:57.980
Victory!

00:22:58.370 --> 00:22:59.700
Victory!
